-12T13:15:08Z","closed_at":"2026-03-12T13:14:17Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Godot v4.6\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.1.stable - Fedora Linux 43 (KDE Plasma Desktop Edition) on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1650 (nvidia; 580.126.18) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-10400 CPU @ 2.90GHz (12 threads) - 15.41 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/220732db-4aff-4a85-9685-d4c7d83194be\n\n`area.get_parent()` returns the `SceneNode` instead of `Foo`, even though `area.get_path()` output is correct. Giving `Foo` another parent doesn't change anything.\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create a project and an empty scene\n- Rename the root node to `SceneNode`\n- Create an `Area2D`, name it `SearcherForFoo`\n- Create a node named Foo\n- Add a child `Area2D`, name it `FooArea`\n- Attach collision shapes to `SearcherForFoo` and `FooArea`\n- Attach a script to `SearcherForFoo`\n- Attach either _on_area_entered or _on_area_shape_entered signal\nin the attached function, write `print(get_parent())`\n- Run the project and move `SearcherForFoo` into `FooArea`\n- `SceneNode` will be printed\n\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[MRP.tar.gz](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25933175/MRP.tar.gz)","closed_by":{"login":"Sungle4232","id":83569242,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTY5MjQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83569242?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sungle4232","html_url":"https://github.com/Sungle4232","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sungle4232/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sungle4232/follo